    {
      "ts": 1791910710.8241663,
      "type": "plan_text",
      "claim_id": "disc_2307_03756_mse",
      "text": "\n\n- **Model**: FITS (Frequency Interpolation Time Series Forecasting) – seq_len = 90, pred_len = 96, enc_in = 7 (ETTh1 channels), individual = False (uncertain), cut_freq = seq_len⁄24 ≈ 3 (uncertain).  \n- **Architecture**: RevIN → real‑FFT → zero‑out frequencies > dominance_freq → linear upsampler (shared if !individual) → zero‑pad to full spectrum → iFFT → multiply by length_ratio → add back RevIN mean/std.  \n- **Hyper‑parameters (from paper/code)**: batch_size = 32, learning_rate = 0.001 (uncertain), weight_decay = 0 (uncertain), epochs = 10 (uncertain), patience = 3 (uncertain), optimizer = Adam, loss = MSE.  \n- **LR schedule**: lr ← lr × 0.95 each epoch after the first (as in `adjust_learning_rate`) (uncertain).  \n- **Dropout**: none in the FITS block (p = 0) (uncertain).  \n- **Hidden size / layers**: no hidden layers; the upsampler maps `dominance_freq` → `dominance_freq × length_ratio` (dimensions derived from seq_len/pred_len) (uncertain).  \n- **Training**: fit on `data[\"train\"]`; use `data[\"val\"]` for validation, holding out the final 20 % of validation samples for early‑stopping checkpoint selection.  \n- **Seed**: read `os.environ[\"SEED\"]`, set `numpy.random.seed` and `torch.manual_seed`.  \n- **Normalization**: data already z‑scored with training mean/std; model applies RevIN internally, no extra scaling.  \n- **Inference**: `model.eval()`, deterministic forward, returns a `[96,7]` NumPy array (or torch tensor converted to NumPy).  \n- **Checkpointing**: best model saved to `/tmp/forecast-agent/checkpoint.pth` and re‑loaded before returning the predictor.  \n- **Budget**: whole procedure (training + validation) finishes < 5 minutes on CPU."
    },
